<mistergamedescription>
	<rbf>_Other/MalditaCastilla</rbf>
</mistergamedescription>
<!--
  Maldita Castilla - Cores-browser entry.
  Installed by deploy.py to /media/fat/_Other/Maldita Castilla.mgl.

  WHY THIS EXISTS: the RBF carries its build date in its name
  (MalditaCastilla_YYYYMMDD.rbf), so the entry the user sees in the Cores
  browser would change on every rebuild. This gives it one stable name.

  WHY IT NEEDS NO DEPLOY-TIME REWRITING: the rbf tag is a PREFIX, not a path.
  MiSTer's get_rbf() (support/arcade/mra_loader.cpp:1223-1296) resolves the
  directory from the storage root, then scans it for .rbf files whose name
  starts with that prefix AND whose next character is '.' or '_', keeping the
  lexicographically greatest match. Since our names sort by date,
  "_Other/MalditaCastilla" always resolves to the NEWEST installed build. Note
  the missing .rbf extension is required, not an omission.

  This on its own only LOADS THE CORE, exactly as selecting the RBF does. What
  starts the engine is whichever trigger is installed: Master_Daemon watching
  /tmp/CORENAME, or the `main=` hook (deploy.py, the main-wrapper flag), which
  needs no daemon. See
  docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-04-hps-takeover-launcher-design.md section 2b.

  Comment placed AFTER the root element and free of double-hyphens: "- -" is
  illegal inside an XML comment, and MiSTer parses this with a real SAX parser
  (sxmlc), not a scanner that would forgive it.
-->
